# Built by build_exe.bat
build/
dist/
*.spec.bak

# Runtime state - the catalogue, the cover cache, whatever the user has rated -
# lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\slgking, not here, so there is normally nothing to
# ignore. Kept as a net for the case where slg_db.app_dir() ever falls back to
# the source tree: that file is personal and must never be committed.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Promo film. tools/make_promo.py and tools/shot_dialogs.py are tracked; the
# frames they render are build output - the mp4 alone is megabytes of dead
# weight in git, and every shot in it is reproducible from the script.
promo/

# Throwaway
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local tooling. .claude/ is this machine's session memory and
# settings, .codepilot-uploads/ is screenshots pasted into chat, and the
# *.ai.md files are generated directory listings. None of it is source.
.claude/
.codepilot-uploads/
README.ai.md
PATH.ai.md

# Server side. The client talks to the author's server, but the deploy tool
# and the catalogue host are single-tenant ops scripts - deploy_server.py alone
# names the host, the SSH port, the login user and the remote layout. They stay
# off the public repo. slg_sync_server.py, despite the name, is the client's
# catalogue puller and is tracked. test_serve_catalog.py imports serve_catalog
# at module level, so it follows them out.
#
# slgking_admin.spec / build_admin.bat are here for the same reason one step
# removed: they build an exe around slg_remote_admin.py, which pulls in all of
# the above.
deploy_server.py
serve_catalog.py
slg_cloud_store.py
slg_moderation.py
cloud_backup.py
admin_page.html
slg_remote_admin.py
slgking_admin.spec
build_admin.bat
tests/test_serve_catalog.py
tests/test_deploy.py
tests/test_cloud_store.py
tests/test_moderation.py
